---
/**
 * foodcraft / HowBO — "Sipsip Tea Bar" HOW IT WORKS (design element
 * data-component="HOW-IT-WORKS", design file line 164).
 *
 * ROLE. The page's one procedural block — how a drink is actually ordered at a
 * bar that has no ordering system. It is the ONLY dark moment in this template:
 * everything above and below it floats on the blush ground, and this section
 * drops a single --ink plate at radius 36px into the middle of the page and
 * puts three lifted cards inside it. That inversion is the whole point of the
 * band, so the plate is drawn first and every colour inside it is chosen
 * against the plate rather than against the page.
 *
 * DESIGN VALUES, lifted verbatim from "Sipsip Tea Bar Landing.dc.html":
 *   section    max-width 1200 / padding 80px 28px 0     → .wrap + the wrapper's
 *                                                         shared section rule
 *                                                         (see NOT RENDERED)
 *   plate      background #241A22, radius 36px,
 *              padding 52px 46px                        → --ink
 *   head       text-align center, margin-bottom 38px
 *   eyebrow    11px / 700 / .14em caps on a pill,
 *              ground #3D2E37, label #F2C6DA,
 *              padding 8px 16px, radius 100px           → .kick + the lift, see
 *                                                         THE TWO LIFTED GROUNDS
 *   h2         Baloo 2 700, clamp(28px,3.8vw,48px)
 *              /1.08, margin .24em 0 0, #FFF7F2         → .h2 + .sip-how-h2
 *   emphasis   a COLOUR change to #F2C6DA — never an
 *              italic; Baloo 2 has none                  → --pink, see THE
 *                                                         EMPHASIS RULE
 *   grid       repeat(3, minmax(0,1fr)), gap 20px
 *   card       background #2F2229, radius 24px,
 *              padding 28px 26px, text-align center
 *   badge      56×56 circle, ground #F2C6DA,
 *              label #3D1B2C, Baloo 2 24px 700          → --pink / --on-pink
 *   h3         Baloo 2 600, 24px, margin 16px 0 8px,
 *              #FFF7F2                                   → --on-ink
 *   body       14.5px / 1.75, #C3B6BD, margin 0
 *   action     centred, margin-top 34px, btnPink =
 *              the design's own btn base + #F2C6DA
 *              ground + #3D1B2C label                    → .btn.btn--pink
 * Not one literal hex is written in the stylesheet below (R1). Every value the
 * design's btnPink declares — inline-flex, centred, 13px/700, padding 16px 30px,
 * radius 100px, the #F2C6DA ground and the #3D1B2C label — is already carried by
 * the wrapper's `.btn` + `.btn--pink`, which add a min-height of 48px, a 1px
 * transparent border, a gap, a pinned line-height and a transition of their own.
 * So this file adds no button rule at all beyond the full-width wrapping label
 * at 520px.
 *
 * EDITABLE HOOKS (every one declared in components/editor/genericContentSchema.ts
 * — group id "how". A data-field on any other path is a dead hook no sidebar
 * input owns.)
 *   how.tag                  — the pink pill eyebrow
 *   how.headline             — fed with set:html, so an owner can put this
 *                              design's signature colour emphasis inside their
 *                              OWN sentence. Guarded: lib/derive-content-
 *                              defaults.ts supplies no how.headline, so an
 *                              unset value must draw nothing rather than open
 *                              a 38px gap above the grid
 *   how.steps.${i}.title     — ORIGINAL index, see LIST INDEXES
 *   how.steps.${i}.body      — canonical key, spelled in the hook even when the
 *                              stored value arrived as .desc / .description, so
 *                              the first save heals the row onto the schema key
 *   how.cta.text             — the pink button's label, THIS section's own
 *   how.cta.href             — its target, via data-href-field. The schema
 *                              declares how.cta.text as a `link` spec whose
 *                              hrefPath IS how.cta.href, so both halves are
 *                              owned by a real sidebar input. It used to be
 *                              hero.cta1.*, shared with the header, the hero and
 *                              the footer: one string for four buttons, so
 *                              retyping one retyped them all — and one colour
 *                              too, because the v3 picker derives a button's
 *                              SECTION from the leading segment of its field
 *                              path and answered "hero" for all four. On how.cta
 *                              this section is retypable and recolourable on its
 *                              own. Both halves FALL BACK to hero.cta1.* while
 *                              how.cta is unset, so no existing site loses a
 *                              button; the hooks always spell how.cta, so the
 *                              owner's first edit writes there and diverges.
 *
 * DERIVED (computed here, never authored here):
 *   · THE NUMERAL, and this is the decision a reader is most likely to read as
 *     an oversight. The design prints `st.n` — '1', '2', '3' — from its own
 *     three-row demo array. Those are the DESIGNER filling in their own
 *     template. What the design SPECIFIES is the treatment: a 56px pink disc
 *     with a 24px Baloo 2 figure on it, and that treatment is reproduced
 *     exactly while the string is derived from the DISPLAY position. It is
 *     aria-hidden and carries NO data-field, so it can never become a content
 *     key an owner has to maintain, and the list is a real <ol> so the ordinal
 *     still reaches assistive tech through the markup.
 *   · `rows` — only the steps carrying real text, each keeping its ORIGINAL
 *     array index (R6).
 *   · `--sip-how-cols` — the track count follows the DATA, capped at the
 *     design's three. Nothing here would print an empty box (the ground is on
 *     the CARD, not on the track), but two filled steps stretched across three
 *     tracks would leave a third of the plate blank and read as a row whose
 *     last step went missing.
 *   · The <ol> carries an explicit role="list", because `list-style: none` is
 *     exactly what makes Safari/VoiceOver drop list semantics — and the ordinal
 *     reaching assistive tech through the markup is the entire reason the
 *     visible numeral is aria-hidden.
 *
 * THE TWO LIFTED GROUNDS — the one thing in this file worth reviewing. The
 * design's plate is #241A22 (= --ink), its cards are #2F2229 and its eyebrow
 * pill is #3D2E37. Those last two have NO token in PageBO: they are the ink
 * lifted a little toward the paper, and R1 forbids inventing the hex. They are
 * written as exactly that — `rgba(var(--paper-rgb), α)` over the --ink plate —
 * which is token-only and, unlike a frozen hex, stays correct if buildOverrideCss
 * repaints --ink and --paper for a scheme. The alphas were solved against the
 * design's own values and the results COMPUTED, not eyeballed:
 *   card    .045 → #2E242B  (design #2F2229)
 *   eyebrow .10  → #3A3037  (design #3D2E37)
 * The step paragraph's #C3B6BD is the same story in reverse — paper carried
 * most of the way over the card ground — and is written `rgba(var(--paper-rgb),
 * .72)`, which composites to #C4BCBA against the design's #C3B6BD. Flagged for
 * review: three values in this file are token expressions rather than tokens.
 *
 * THE EMPHASIS RULE, and why it is overridden here and nowhere else in this
 * family. PageBO paints `:where(.h2 em)` and `:where(.em)` in --accent, and the
 * purple is right on every other section in this template because every other
 * section is on paper. On THIS plate --accent measures 2.83:1 against --ink —
 * computed, and far under the floor. The design's own emphasis here is the
 * pink, at 11.13:1. The override is reached through :global() because scoped
 * rules cannot touch markup that set:html created (R3), and it out-specifies
 * the wrapper's :where() rule without !important.
 *
 * PINK AS TEXT, once, deliberately. PageBO's header says --pink is a GROUND and
 * never text, and that rule is about the blush page: purple on pink is 3.93:1
 * and pink on paper is worse. On the INK plate the relationship inverts, and
 * the design uses the pink as its text colour in both places it appears —
 * eyebrow and headline emphasis. Both were computed before use (below) and both
 * clear AA comfortably. Nowhere in this file is pink text placed on anything
 * but the ink plate or its lift.
 *
 * ANTI-FABRICATION (R2). Not one word here is written by this file. The
 * design's own steps — "Message us the drinks, sugar and ice levels", "Made to
 * hit your pickup minute so the ice has not melted into it", "Sealed, bagged
 * and waiting at the counter under your name" — are a service promise, a
 * punctuality guarantee and a pickup procedure asserted on behalf of a business
 * nobody has spoken to, so none of them ships. A bar that has said nothing
 * about its process gets no process section at all.
 *
 * SECTION GATE (R5) = rows.length, the BODY content. It cannot count how.tag,
 * because lib/derive-content-defaults.ts hard-codes how.tag to 'How it works'
 * on EVERY site — a gate that counted it would drop a full dark plate carrying
 * an eyebrow and nothing else into the middle of every page that never filled
 * the steps in, which on this design is the single most conspicuous empty
 * element the template can produce. The CTA is not counted either: a section
 * whose only content is a button is a heading over nothing.
 *
 * LIST INDEXES (R6). data-field carries the ORIGINAL index; the numeral, the
 * reveal stagger and the track count use the DISPLAY position, because a
 * decorative figure and a transition delay are decoration. Dropping a blank
 * row 2 therefore renumbers the visible discs but cannot misdirect an edit of
 * row 3 into row 2.
 *
 * ARRAY SOURCE. how.steps is canonical, and the hook ALWAYS spells how.steps —
 * the read-tolerant / write-canonical split every other How section in the repo
 * uses. A legacy site whose rows live under how.items still RENDERS, but its
 * hooks are not re-pointed there: genericContentSchema declares no how.items
 * list and no fallbackPaths for it, so a hook spelled that way would be inert
 * in the sidebar.
 *
 * NOT RENDERED, deliberately:
 *   · NO id on the section. This page's anchors are menu / about / gallery /
 *     visit / faq / main; the design gives HOW-IT-WORKS no id and nothing in
 *     the nav points at it, so inventing #how would add a target nothing aims
 *     for.
 *   · NO SECTION PADDING OF ITS OWN. The design writes `padding: 80px 28px 0`
 *     on this section and lets the NEXT section's top padding be the whole gap;
 *     PageBO instead declares ONE shared symmetric rhythm —
 *     `section { padding: clamp(48px,6.4vw,80px) 0 }` — whose cap is exactly
 *     the design's 80px, and that wrapper rule is the contract all fifteen BO
 *     sections sit on. A top-only padding here would not restore anything:
 *     GalleryBO above still pays its own symmetric bottom, so the space above
 *     the plate is unchanged either way, and the only thing that would move is
 *     that HOW becomes the one section in the variant that butts into the
 *     reviews below it. The horizontal 28px is likewise not restated: `.wrap`
 *     is `min(1200px, 92vw)`, the design's cap and its side air in one
 *     declaration.
 *   · NO .band-pink, NO .band-sage, NO .band-lilac. All three exist in the
 *     wrapper and this section opts into none of them, because the design's
 *     ground here is neither: it is a full-bleed-free --ink PLATE inside a
 *     normal paper section, with the page's blush still visible down both
 *     sides. --ink does carry a declared on-colour in the wrapper — `.plate
 *     .cap` is `background-color: var(--ink); color: var(--on-ink)` — so the
 *     text colour on this plate is still the pairing the wrapper declares and
 *     not one this file invented.
 *   · NO focus-ring override. The wrapper's indicator is a 3px --paper outline
 *     with a 6px --accent halo outside it, and --paper against --ink is 15.92:1
 *     (PageBO's own computed figure), so the ring reads on the dark plate
 *     without help. The wrapper's one override exists for .band-pink, which
 *     this section does not use.
 *   · NO .body primitive on the step paragraph. .body is
 *     clamp(14.5px,1.3vw,15.5px) / 1.72 / --ink-soft; the design's paragraph is
 *     a flat 14.5 / 1.75 in a light grey that only exists on the dark plate, so
 *     all three of those would have been overridden. A section that overrides
 *     three of a primitive's properties is not reusing it. font-family is left
 *     to inherit var(--sans) from body, exactly as it does in the design.
 *   · NO star row, NO rating, NO photo, NO role="img", NO .plate, NO .cap. This
 *     section has none in the design, so R2's rating rule and R9's accessible
 *     name have nothing to bind to here.
 *   · NO `target="_blank"` on an in-page action. The design hard-codes one
 *     because its own href is a Messenger URL, but the same button may now
 *     resolve to '#visit', and opening an in-page anchor in a new tab is a bug.
 *     Emitted for http(s) only.
 *   · NO cap on the headline measure. The wrapper's .h2 caps itself at 22ch,
 *     which is right for this template's LEFT-aligned headlines; this one is
 *     centred by its parent, and a 22ch block with no auto margins would hug
 *     the left edge of the plate while centring its text inside itself. The
 *     design states no cap on this h2, so the cap is removed rather than
 *     converted to `margin-inline: auto`.
 *
 * RESPONSIVE (R8). The wrapper owns the shared 760 / 520 type pass; the grid
 * and the plate below are this section's. THE ONLY CLAMP IN THIS FILE is the
 * headline's, and it is declared ONCE at base and never restated in a query,
 * so the ladder cannot invert: clamp(28px,3.8vw,48px) reads its 48px cap from
 * ~1263px up, 45.6 at 1200, 34.2 at 900, 28.88 at 760 and its 28px floor from
 * ~737px down. Note that this scoped rule also out-specifies the wrapper's own
 * 760 `.h2` rule (a :where() selector at 0,1,1 against this file's 0,2,0), so
 * that clamp(26px,7vw,29px) step never applies here. This file's own curve runs
 * straight through the boundary — 28.918px at 761, 28.88 at 760 — so nothing
 * jumps either way: the wrapper's step would have drawn 29px there, and below
 * 400px its 7vw term falls BELOW this file's flat 28px floor instead. Winning
 * the specificity fight is therefore not uniformly "smaller"; what it buys is
 * that ONE monotonic curve governs at every width. Every other size in this
 * file is flat, and every type and spacing value in the 900 and 520 queries is
 * below the one it replaces. The single value that GROWS in a query is the
 * action button's width at 520, which goes full-bleed: it fills the column it
 * already sits in rather than exceeding it, and it is the reason that rule also
 * carries white-space + overflow-wrap.
 *
 * CONTRAST, COMPUTED from the hexes PageBO declares (sRGB relative luminance,
 * WCAG 2.x) with the two lifts and the translucent body colour composited
 * first, rather than estimated:
 *   --on-ink on --ink (the plate)                     15.92
 *   --on-ink on the card lift (the step titles)       14.14
 *   --pink on --ink (the headline emphasis)           11.13
 *   --pink on the eyebrow lift                         8.36
 *   rgba(--paper-rgb,.72) on the card lift (the body)  8.02
 *   --on-pink on --pink (the disc, and the button)     9.96
 * Caveat, the same one PageBO makes for --muted: buildOverrideCss owns --ink,
 * --on-ink and --paper-rgb and wins them with !important, so the first five
 * figures are the NATIVE palette's. The pairing itself is structural — paper
 * carried over ink — and stays a light-on-dark pair under any scheme, but the
 * exact numbers are not a guarantee. --pink and --on-pink are invisible to that
 * file, so the last figure holds everywhere.
 *
 * SCOPING (R3). One scoped <style> block, no is:global; the single :global() is
 * the emphasis rule, which has to reach set:html output. Classes are prefixed
 * sip-how- for THIS template and are not a sibling's names re-used: an audit
 * had to rename a whole set copied verbatim between two files in this family,
 * so nothing here reuses HowBM's hbm- or HowBL's how- names. Button classes are
 * .btn / .btn--pink only — buildOverrideCss pins label colours on .btn-primary
 * / .btn-ghost / .nav-cta / .cta-band .btn / .testi .btn with !important, and
 * none of those selectors reaches anything here (R4).
 */
// `layout` is accepted because PageBO passes it to every section uniformly;
// this block reads nothing outside content.*.
interface Props { content: any; layout?: any; }
const { content } = Astro.props;

const how = content?.how || {};
const tag = typeof how.tag === 'string' ? how.tag.trim() : '';
// Trimmed and otherwise untouched: this goes out through set:html, so whatever
// markup the owner typed reaches the emphasis rule intact.
const headline = typeof how.headline === 'string' ? how.headline.trim() : '';

type Step = { title?: string; body?: string; desc?: string; description?: string };
// Read tolerantly — a legacy site stores its rows under how.items — and write
// canonically. See ARRAY SOURCE above.
const source: Step[] = Array.isArray(how.steps)
  ? how.steps
  : (Array.isArray(how.items) ? how.items : []);
const titleOf = (s: Step): string => String(s?.title ?? '').trim();
const bodyOf = (s: Step): string => String(s?.body ?? s?.desc ?? s?.description ?? '').trim();
// A step the admin added but never filled would otherwise print a 56px pink
// disc over nothing inside a lifted card, and a title of pure whitespace would
// ship an empty <h3>. Normalise first, drop the blanks (whitespace counts as
// blank) and keep the ORIGINAL index on every survivor.
const rows = source
  .map((s, i: number) => ({ i, title: titleOf(s), body: bodyOf(s) }))
  .filter((r) => Boolean(r.title || r.body));

// Track count follows the DATA, capped at the design's three. Three or more
// filled steps compute exactly the design's repeat(3, minmax(0,1fr)); a fourth
// and beyond wrap onto a second row of cards.
const cols = String(Math.min(Math.max(rows.length, 1), 3));

// Anchor guard (R7). Resolve in-page hrefs against the ids PageBO actually
// renders — menu, about, gallery, visit, faq, main — and remap what
// derive-content-defaults emits onto them: the services block IS the drinks
// menu (rooms lands there too), '#about' is the shop's own story (host and why
// are the same block here), '#work' is the photo wall, '#location' and
// '#contact' both mean the visit block, and a booking link has no checkout to
// reach on this page so it lands on <main>. Off-page hrefs — tel:, mailto:,
// http(s) and anything else without a leading '#' — pass through untouched.
// Keep this table in step with the copies in the other BO sections.
const PAGE_ANCHORS = new Set(['menu', 'about', 'gallery', 'visit', 'faq', 'main']);
const ANCHOR_ALIAS: Record<string, string> = {
  book: 'main',
  contact: 'visit',
  host: 'about',
  location: 'visit',
  rooms: 'menu',
  services: 'menu',
  why: 'about',
  work: 'gallery',
};
const onPage = (href: string | undefined, fallback: string): string => {
  if (!href) return fallback;
  if (!href.startsWith('#')) return href;
  const id = href.slice(1);
  if (PAGE_ANCHORS.has(id)) return href;
  const alias = ANCHOR_ALIAS[id];
  return alias && PAGE_ANCHORS.has(alias) ? `#${alias}` : fallback;
};

const hero = content?.hero || {};
// THIS SECTION'S OWN button. how.cta is read FIRST; the hero's primary action is
// the FALLBACK, and the fallback half is byte-for-byte the expression this file
// used before the split — so a site that never sets how.cta renders identically.
// The hooks below always spell how.cta, which is what makes the first edit
// diverge instead of retyping the header, the hero and the footer with it.
const ownCtaText = typeof how.cta?.text === 'string' ? how.cta.text.trim() : '';
const ctaText = ownCtaText || (typeof hero.cta1?.text === 'string' ? hero.cta1.text.trim() : '');
// #visit is where this template puts the address, the map and the opening
// hours, so it is the honest landing place for an action that cannot be
// resolved — the last step above it has just told the visitor to come and
// collect the order.
const ctaHref = onPage(how.cta?.href || hero.cta1?.href, '#visit');
// Carried for http(s) ONLY — see NOT RENDERED above.
const ctaExternal = /^https?:/i.test(ctaHref);
---
{rows.length > 0 && (
  <section class="sip-how">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sip-how-plate">
        {(tag || headline) && (
          <div class="sip-how-head reveal">
            {tag && <span class="kick sip-how-kick" data-field="how.tag">{tag}</span>}
            {headline && <h2 class="h2 sip-how-h2" data-field="how.headline" set:html={headline}></h2>}
          </div>
        )}

        <ol class="sip-how-grid" role="list" style={`--sip-how-cols:${cols}`}>
          {rows.map((step, k) => (
            <li class="sip-how-card reveal" data-delay={String(Math.min(k, 3))}>
              {/* DERIVED chrome: the DISPLAY position, aria-hidden, no
                  data-field. The <ol> already carries the ordinal for
                  assistive tech. */}
              <span class="fig sip-how-n" aria-hidden="true">{String(k + 1)}</span>
              {step.title && <h3 class="sip-how-t" data-field={`how.steps.${step.i}.title`}>{step.title}</h3>}
              {step.body && <p class="sip-how-p" data-field={`how.steps.${step.i}.body`}>{step.body}</p>}
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>

        {ctaText && (
          <div class="sip-how-act reveal">
            <a
              class="btn btn--pink"
              href={ctaHref}
              target={ctaExternal ? '_blank' : undefined}
              rel={ctaExternal ? 'noopener noreferrer' : undefined}
              data-field="how.cta.text"
              data-href-field="how.cta.href"
            >{ctaText}</a>
          </div>
        )}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
)}
<style>
  /* Colour and type come only from PageBO's token vocabulary — --ink --on-ink
     --pink --on-pink --paper-rgb --r-pill --disp --sans, plus .wrap, .kick,
     .h2, .fig, .btn and .btn--pink. There is not one literal hex in this file
     (R1); the three values the design draws that have no token are written as
     token expressions over --ink, documented in the frontmatter.

     (Never write a literal end-style-tag inside a comment in here — the parser
      would end the stylesheet on the spot and silently truncate the file.) */

  /* The section states NO vertical padding and NO measure: both are the
     wrapper's, and its `section` cap is exactly the design's 80px. See the
     frontmatter for why a top-only padding here would buy nothing. */

  /* THE PLATE — the page's one dark ground. --ink with the wrapper's own
     declared on-colour for it, so nothing inside has to guess.
     36px is a LENGTH, not a colour: R1 governs colour, and no token holds 36
     (--r-lg is 26, --r-md is 18, --r-pill is 100), so the design's number
     stands rather than being rounded to a different drawing. */
  .sip-how-plate {
    background-color: var(--ink);
    color: var(--on-ink);
    border-radius: 36px;
    padding: 52px 46px;
  }

  /* Design: centred header, margin-bottom 38px. The margin lives on the block
     rather than on the h2, so the gap above the grid is identical whether or
     not the owner typed a headline — and derive-content-defaults ships how.tag
     on every site but NO how.headline, so "eyebrow, then straight into the
     grid" is the DEFAULT state, not an edge case. */
  .sip-how-head { text-align: center; margin-bottom: 38px; }

  /* The eyebrow keeps .kick's 11px / 700 / uppercase and its tight line box;
     what is local is the design's .14em tracking, the pill, and the colours.
     The colours MUST be local: .kick is --accent, and purple on this plate is
     2.83:1. The ground is the ink lifted a tenth of the way to paper — the
     design's own eyebrow ground — written as a token expression so it
     tracks --ink. The hex it solves against is in the frontmatter table.
     max-width and overflow-wrap because the tag is owner-typed and one
     unbroken word in .14em caps would otherwise be the widest thing here. */
  .sip-how-head .sip-how-kick {
    letter-spacing: .14em;
    color: var(--pink);
    background-color: rgba(var(--paper-rgb), .10);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: var(--r-pill);
    max-width: 100%;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  /* Design: Baloo 2 700 (from the wrapper's .h2), clamp(28px,3.8vw,48px) / 1.08,
     margin .24em 0 0, and the paper-white ink. The colour has to be restated
     because the
     wrapper's shared h1-h4 reset paints --ink, which is the ground here. The
     cap is removed rather than made auto-margined — see NOT RENDERED.
     This is the file's ONLY clamp and it is declared once; see RESPONSIVE. */
  .sip-how-h2 {
    font-size: clamp(28px, 3.8vw, 48px);
    line-height: 1.08;
    margin: .24em 0 0;
    max-width: none;
    color: var(--on-ink);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  /* THE EMPHASIS. PageBO paints .h2 em / .em in --accent, which is right on
     paper and 2.83:1 on this plate. The design's emphasis here is the pink, at
     11.13:1. :global() because scoped rules cannot reach markup that set:html
     created (R3); font-style stays normal because Baloo 2 has no italic and a
     synthesised oblique fights its rounded terminals. */
  .sip-how-h2 :global(em),
  .sip-how-h2 :global(.em) {
    font-style: normal;
    color: var(--pink);
  }

  /* Design: three equal tracks at a 20px gutter, following the DATA up to
     three. minmax(0,1fr) rather than 1fr so a long unbroken word in a step
     cannot widen its own track and push the page sideways. The inline custom
     property sets no grid-template-columns of its own, so the 900px rule below
     still wins on source order. */
  .sip-how-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(var(--sip-how-cols, 1), minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 20px;
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  /* Design: the lifted card ground, radius 24px, padding 28px 26px, centred.
     The ground is the
     ink lifted ~4.5% toward paper — see the frontmatter. min-width:0 as well as
     the minmax() above, because a grid item's default min-width is auto. */
  .sip-how-card {
    min-width: 0;
    background-color: rgba(var(--paper-rgb), .045);
    border-radius: 24px;
